nodes.prompt:
You are a careful mathematical solver. Produce an initial complete attempt at solving the problem stated below. Use rigorous reasoning; show your work step-by-step; state every non-trivial intermediate claim with a short justification. End with a clearly labelled final answer.

PROBLEM:
${INPUT}

You are reviewing your own draft solution. Take the prior solution below and produce an IMPROVED version that: (a) fixes any logical gaps, (b) tightens notation, (c) adds missing justifications, (d) preserves the original mathematical argument unless you have a strong reason to change it. Return the full improved solution, not just edits.

PRIOR SOLUTION:
${ARTIFACT}

The verifier flagged issues with the current solution. Below is the verifier's structured critique (a JSON object with verdict, severity, and issues). Analyse the issues, decide which are real bugs versus surface issues, and produce a concise BUG REPORT enumerating the load-bearing problems the corrector should address. Order them by priority (most critical first). Do NOT attempt to fix anything yourself; only enumerate.

VERIFIER CRITIQUE:
${CRITIQUE}

You are correcting a flawed mathematical solution. Below is the current solution followed by a prioritised bug report. Apply the corrections implied by the bug report. Preserve the correct parts of the prior argument; rewrite only what needs rewriting. Return the full corrected solution.

CURRENT SOLUTION:
${ARTIFACT}

BUG REPORT:
${INPUT}
